ayload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"39fe4f36e48a35482603ba91371c473fc87f31af09f83d3c280f40514247d255","event_uuid":"3ebfa887-bf23-4dbe-86da-e4c5ea8e2b10","position":{"commit_sha":"139e8a53eb8c644e4f74f14d6e2dd719e5869f67","position":"1788588039504411001-3ebfa887-bf23-4dbe-86da-e4c5ea8e2b10"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d4ef74b2cc0de0b824154e5db93373683d6a6ce61f2ea1d3a1b1c7c4fa1e3f2f","event_uuid":"10760601-8389-4c39-9449-e8986a4c0a88","position":{"commit_sha":"08c8912ae94fb80cb5ef7b7036ecd18af04e481e","position":"1788588122098503001-10760601-8389-4c39-9449-e8986a4c0a88"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan-review PASS (attempt 4) after remediating: ADR collision (now amends 0115, no new 0111), receipt-schema/enum extension stated + schema in file_impact, and Scope now enumerates all wiring edit targets (terraform_tools/terraform_seam/terraform_receipt + receipt schema) with those two consumers added to file_impact (13 paths). Portability clause added for Windows fallback. Claimed; beginning held-out TDD. Non-blocking advisories to fold during impl: E1 (list ADR/docs in Scope edit targets), T3 (verify the pinned terraform-config-inspect commit ships a runnable CLI accepting --json <snapshot> positionally BEFORE building the full adapter — it is primarily the Go library tfconfig).","timestamp":1788588039504411001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"T3 verified from upstream source (pinned commit main.go): --json is a spf13/pflag bool, the snapshot dir is positional flag.Arg(0), module JSON is written to stdout via MarshalIndent(+newline), and exit code 1 signals module.Diagnostics.HasErrors(). Confirms the invocation surface 'terraform-config-inspect --json <snapshot>' (positional snapshot; --after-init/--stack correctly forbidden — --after-init reads .terraform). Nonzero exit → abstain aligns with diagnostics-present. CI canary lane still exercises the real binary. No local Go toolchain, so source inspection substitutes for the pre-build probe.","timestamp":1788588122098503001}],"created_at":1788470032489544433,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"39c94895-fa12-4cd7-a0a3-e0c68987642b","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"1c52-5e73-4d61-4124"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe prior slices establish a bounded structural index and Terraform-only tool sessions in both review pipelines [rebar:depraved-classless-rooster]. This slice adds optional independent corroboration from HashiCorp's `terraform-config-inspect` when it is already on `PATH`. Audited basis: commit `2fb54c23…` (full sha in Verification), whose shallow loader extracts top-level metadata with a nil expression context and runs no Terraform.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd `src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py` and expose `corroborate_diagnostic(module, diagnostic, subject, expected=None)` in both pipelines. Edit targets: the session method in `terraform_tools.py`; fourth-tool registration in `terraform_seam.py` `_session_tools` (the shared minting site both pipelines consume); receipt + `match`-outcome handling in `terraform_receipt.py`; the `operation`/`outcome` enum extension in `terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json`.\n\n### Closed query and result contract\n\nAccepted diagnostics are:\n\n- `declaration_present`: named variable, output, managed resource, data resource, module call, or required provider.\n- `module_source_equals`: a named module call has the normalized expected literal source.\n- `required_provider_present`: a named provider requirement exists.\n\nAn exact schema-valid entry returns `match` at T1. Missing or unequal entries, absence claims, and unsupported/computed semantics return `abstain`; upstream silence never proves correctness or absence. Results contain only normalized names, classes, positions, and hashes — never descriptions, defaults, constraints, diagnostics, or upstream literal payloads. `match` is emitted only by the corroborator; the refutation-only ops stay `refuted`/`abstain`.\n\n### Hardened execution\n\n- Resolve only the exact `terraform-config-inspect` basename from inherited `PATH`; canonicalize once and reject non-regular/non-executable or repo/snapshot-contained candidates. Invoke its absolute path without a shell using only `--json <snapshot>`; never pass `--after-init`, `--stack`, repository arguments, or shell text.\n- Copy the immutable indexed whole-module bytes into a fresh directory: regular `.tf` and `.tf.json` files only, no symlinks. Make it read-only, run there, and never pass the repository path.\n- Close stdin, create a process group/session, and allow only locale, OS-required process variables, and temporary `HOME`/`TMPDIR`. Strip Terraform/OpenTofu, provider/cloud credential, proxy, plugin, CLI-config, and repository variables.\n- Apply the existing 60-second deadline; cap stdout at 4 MiB and stderr at 64 KiB. On timeout, overflow, cancellation, or error, terminate then kill and reap the whole group and remove the snapshot; on non-POSIX platforms (e.g. Windows) lacking process-group/session semantics, use the stdlib's cross-platform terminate→kill under the same deadline. Hash the executable before and after; replacement abstains.\n- Record backend, canonical path, SHA-256, discoverable version or `unknown`, invocation profile, snapshot digest, normalized query, outcome, and result digest. Never log child streams or environment values.\n\nValidate stdout against a Rebar-owned schema for the audited JSON fields; every reported filename must name a copied snapshot file. Unknown/malformed shapes, upstream diagnostics, nonzero exit, overflow, path mismatch, binary replacement, or schema skew (upstream JSON failing that schema) produce one closed abstention with no partial facts. A `match` is gated on schema validity, never the version string: the version is provenance-only and the binary is pinned by SHA-256 (hashed before/after). A corroborator can strengthen a positive Pass-1 fact or independently support Pass-2; it cannot originate a finding, veto ordinary review, or turn abstention into negative evidence.\n\n### Pinned upstream canary\n\nExtend the optionality workflow with a gating lane that installs the pinned `terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c23…` commit, exposes only that binary on the test `PATH`, and drives the real adapter over a full-declaration module. Assert positive matches, absence-as-abstention, schema acceptance, provenance, and cleanup. Normal unit tests remain network-free and substitute an executable fixture only at the process boundary.\n\n## Positive rationale\n\nHashiCorp's shallow extractor is a narrow authoritative cross-check; match-only semantics and the minimal snapshot/fixed process contract keep config, plugins, cached modules, and credentials from corrupting it.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nTerraform/OpenTofu and provider execution; validate/plan/init/get; TFLint, Trivy, tfparse, terraform-ls, terraform-docs; module fetch; after-init/stack modes; arbitrary diagnostics; absence claims; expression evaluation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Unit tests through the production adapter prove the closed diagnostic enum and exact-match T1 outcomes for every supported class; missing, unequal, absence-claim, and computed controls return `abstain`.\n- [ ] Parent/child subprocess tests capture argv, cwd, stdin, environment, permissions, and bytes, proving only canonical `terraform-config-inspect --json <snapshot>` launches and no repo path, symlink, credential/config variable, or forbidden executable reaches it.\n- [ ] Timeout, overflow, cancellation, nonzero-exit, and parser-failure faults observe process-group reaping and snapshot removal before return; a clean retry succeeds.\n- [ ] Producer/consumer contract tests prove diagnostics, unknown/malformed fields, escaping filenames, changed binary digests, and version/schema skew yield one redacted abstention without partial facts.\n- [ ] Receipt tests assert provenance fields and byte-scan results, receipts, logs, and exceptions to prove fixture literals, credentials, streams, and environment values never escape.\n- [ ] Terraform plan-review and code-review Pass 1/Pass 2 advertise `corroborate_diagnostic`; non-IaC and missing-extra sessions do not, and abstention leaves the ordinary decision path unchanged.\n- [ ] The optionality workflow runs the real adapter against the exact audited commit and fails on drift; `docs/grounding.md` gives the same opt-in local canary.\n- [ ] ADR 0115 (the established Terraform structural-grounding ADR, already amended by 1c52) gains a new section recording the `terraform-config-inspect` executable trust boundary, audited commit, match-only semantics, and the standing prohibition on every other Terraform-related executable. No new ADR number is allocated (0111/0116 are taken).\n\n## Testing\n\nTest contract card:\n\n- Contract: REB-640, upstream README/JSON at the pinned commit, [rebar:depraved-classless-rooster].\n- Preconditions: indexed module; executable fixtures for success, skew, secret-bearing output, overflow, hang, signal-resistant child, self-replacement; pinned real binary in the canary.\n- Production path (unit tests replace only the executable): real snapshot, discovery, launcher, bounded capture, schema parser, receipt, routing — across schema-unit, real parent/child subprocess, workflow-integration, and live-upstream-canary tiers.\n- Oracles: exact outcome/tier/reason; captured child contract; child absent + snapshot removed + retry OK; exact receipt; byte-level non-disclosure. Negative controls: exact positive matches, nearest absence/inequality abstains, non-Terraform routes expose no tool. CI: `make test` + gating pinned-upstream canary.\n\n## Verification\n\n`env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py`\n\nAC7/AC8 pinned canary (gating; same opt-in command in `docs/grounding.md`):\n\n`go install github.com/hashicorp/terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d && env PATH=\"$(go env GOPATH)/bin:$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" REBAR_TERRAFORM_CONFIG_INSPECT_CANARY=1 python -m pytest tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py -k pinned_upstream_canary`","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py","reason":"hardened PATH discovery, immutable snapshot, bounded subprocess, schema parsing, match-only evidence, and provenance"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_tools.py","reason":"expose corroborate_diagnostic through established Terraform-scoped sessions"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/terraform_config_inspect.schema.json","reason":"pin the accepted upstream JSON producer contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py","reason":"query enum, schema, redaction, process containment, cleanup, and fault oracles"},{"path":"tests/fixtures/terraform_config_inspect/","reason":"production-shaped module used by the fake and real upstream contract paths"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_plan_review_tools.py","reason":"plan-review Pass-1/Pass-2 visibility and abstention integration"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_terraform_code_review_tools.py","reason":"code-review IaC Pass-1/Pass-2 visibility and abstention integration"},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"install and gate against the exact audited upstream commit"},{"path":"docs/adr/0115-terraform-structural-grounding.md","reason":"amend the established Terraform structural-grounding ADR with the terraform-config-inspect executable trust boundary, audited commit, and match-only semantics (no new ADR number: 0111/0116 are taken)"},{"path":"docs/grounding.md","reason":"document optional availability, provenance, abstentions, and local canary"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/terraform_grounding_receipt.schema.json","reason":"extend the closed receipt schema so the corroborator can be represented: add corroborate_diagnostic to the operation enum and match to the outcome enum, guarded so only the corroborator may emit match"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/terraform_seam.py","reason":"register terraform_corroborate_diagnostic as the fourth session tool in _session_tools, the single shared minting site both Pass-1 and Pass-2 pipelines consume"},{"path":"src/rebar/grounding/terraform_receipt.py","reason":"construct the corroborator receipt and extend the ABSTENTIONS/outcome handling for the new match outcome and reason_details"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","1c52-5e73-4d61-4124"],["parent","a374-849c-c8f2-4234"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","parent_status_uuid":"05a8b39b-7f4c-4d0a-b1b8-